<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Oil and Gas abandons Ruby-1.</title>
<headline>NZ Oil and Gas abandons Ruby-1.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand Oil and Gas Ltd said on Friday its Ruby-1 exploration well in Western Australia had been abandoned as a dry well.</p>
<p>Since Tuesday, intermediate electric logging was completed and the well drilled to a total depth of 500 metres.</p>
<p>Minor dry gas peaks were encountered while drilling this section, but after running electric logs, evaluation indicated that no significant hydrocarbon bearing zones were present.</p>
<p>Ruby-1 is 15 km south of the Tubridgi Gas Field.</p>
<p>- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734746</p>
</text>
